  "generatedAt": "2026-10-03T02:04:36.805Z",
  "title": "Symlink-safe scanning, agent rules split by folder, and skill linting in CI",
  "summary": "This change does three things at once. First, `osf scan` stops following symlinks: `collect_files` now uses `symlink_metadata` and counts a link as skipped instead of reading the file or directory it points at, so a link that cycles back on itself can no longer recurse forever and a scan of nothing but links is never reported as clean. Second, the agent-facing rules are reorganised: the root `AGENTS.md` keeps only cross-cutting rules, folder-scoped rules move into `crates/AGENTS.md` and `.github/workflows/AGENTS.md`, and seven new skills under `.agents/skills/` carry the moment-of-work rules, with `.claude/skills` kept as a git symlink to that folder. Third, CI gains two steps in the `rust` job that lint every skill folder and assert that `.claude/skills` is still a symlink to `../.agents/skills`.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
